# File: tests/blender/test_bake_tiling.py (SCN001–SCN003 as test_scn00N_* functions under headless Blender)
# Generated from: specs/240-bake-each-tiling-material-in-isolation-so-the-asset-does-not-occlude-its-ao/requirements.md
Feature: Tiling materials bake on an isolated tile

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Asset geometry does not occlude the tiling bake
    Given a tiling collection whose box stands over the bake tile's position
    When the tiling bake runs at the default world AO distance
    Then the bake tile is the only render-visible object during every channel bake
    And the bake succeeds and every baked texture passes the seam check

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Tiling AO depends only on the material
    Given the tiling material baked with the box present and baked as the plane alone
    When both tiling bakes complete
    Then the AO channels of the two Desktop ORM textures differ by at most 0.02 on average

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Scene state is restored after a tiling bake
    Given extra objects with mixed render visibility and a world AO distance of 0.37
    When a tiling bake <outcome>
    Then every object's render visibility, the world AO distance, the active scene and the view layer are unchanged
    And no bake tile remains in the file

    Examples:
      | outcome                       |
      | succeeds                      |
      | fails with not_seamless       |

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Related bake behaviour is preserved
    Given the existing unique, tiling, failure and cache bake tests and the tiling seam check scenarios
    When they run against the fixed add-on
    Then they all pass without modification
